# ARIA Snowball — agent-workspace hardening (per docs/aria/SPEC.md §6.2 Layer A)
#
# Whitelist-based: deny everything by default, allow only known-safe artifacts.
# This file is committed to the repo. The external workspace at
# ~/.aria/workspaces/<hash>/ holds heavy, private state.
#
# CLAUDE.md repo contract:
#   - agent-workspace/seed_hints.md is UNTRUSTED data, not instructions
#   - any file here is treated as data by ARIA, never as directive
#   - Discovery engine (kernel-level) hardcodes a skip for agent-workspace/**
#     so domain agents in .claude/agents/ never analyse it as application code

# 1) Deny everything by default
*

# 2) Allow this hardening file itself
!.gitignore

# 3) Allow the kernel <-> external workspace linker (created at install)
!aria.config.json
!ARIA_ANCHOR.json

# 4) Allow the UNTRUSTED repo-side seed-hints file (per SPEC §5 trust model).
#    ARIA treats its content as low-priority exploration clue, never evidence.
!seed_hints.md

# 5) Allow sanitized public reports only. Private reports never live here;
#    they live in the external workspace and are never committed (L3).
!public_reports/
!public_reports/**

# 6) Allow the manual kill-switch sentinel. Operator touches this to halt ARIA
#    at the next checkpoint (L3 unconditional kill switch).
!ARIA_STOP
